---
title: Text effects
description: Decoration for a headline, as single classes. Put one on the heading, or on a span around a few words. Each degrades to plain text, and all motion stops under reduced motion.
eyebrow: Effects
source: src/effects/text.css · src/js/im-motion.js
---
<h2>Gradient</h2>
{{#example}}
<p class="text-display font-semibold tracking-tighter"><span class="im-fx-gradient">Ink into accent.</span></p>
<p class="text-h1 font-semibold tracking-tight mt-4"><span class="im-fx-gradient" style="--im-fx-from: var(--im-info); --im-fx-to: var(--im-success); --im-fx-angle: 90deg">Any two colours, any angle.</span></p>
{{/example}}
<p><code>--im-fx-from</code>, <code>--im-fx-to</code>, <code>--im-fx-angle</code>. The text must stay legible at both ends of the gradient — check the lighter end against the background.</p>

<h2>Shine</h2>
{{#example}}
<p class="text-display font-semibold tracking-tighter"><span class="im-fx-shine">A light passes over it.</span></p>
{{/example}}
<p>A highlight sweeps across, forever. <code>--im-fx-speed</code> (3.2s). For a word that is loading, or one line on a launch page — not for body copy.</p>

<h2>Outline</h2>
{{#example}}
<p class="text-display font-bold tracking-tighter"><span class="im-fx-outline">Stroke, no fill.</span></p>
<p class="text-display font-bold tracking-tighter mt-2"><span class="im-fx-outline im-fx-outline-fill">Hover to fill me.</span></p>
{{/example}}
<p><code>--im-fx-stroke</code> (1.5px). Needs a heavy weight and a large size; thin outlined text is unreadable.</p>

<h2>Highlighter</h2>
{{#example}}
<p class="text-h1 font-semibold tracking-tight" data-im-reveal="none" style="max-width: 24ch">The part that matters is <span class="im-fx-marker">run over with a yellow highlighter</span> as you reach it.</p>
<p class="text-lg mt-6 leading-loose">Other inks: <span class="im-fx-marker im-fx-marker-on">yellow</span>, <span class="im-fx-marker im-fx-marker-pink im-fx-marker-on">pink</span>, <span class="im-fx-marker im-fx-marker-green im-fx-marker-on">green</span>, <span class="im-fx-marker im-fx-marker-blue im-fx-marker-on">blue</span>, <span class="im-fx-marker im-fx-marker-accent im-fx-marker-on">the accent</span> — and <span class="im-fx-marker im-fx-marker-full im-fx-marker-on">full height</span>, a swipe over the whole line.</p>
{{/example}}
<p><code>im-fx-marker</code> is highlighter <strong>yellow</strong> by default, with slightly slanted, uneven ends like a real pen stroke. It draws itself when an ancestor with <code>data-im-reveal</code> is revealed, or on hover; <code>im-fx-marker-on</code> keeps it on. The ink is behind the words and re-mixed for dark mode, so the text keeps its own colour and stays readable. It follows the text across line breaks.</p>

<h2>Hand-drawn circle</h2>
{{#example}}
<p class="text-display font-semibold tracking-tighter" style="max-width: 16ch">Draw a <span data-im-scribble="circle">circle</span> round the word that matters.</p>
<p class="text-h2 font-semibold tracking-tight mt-8">Or <span data-im-scribble="underline">underline it</span>, <span data-im-scribble="box" style="--im-fx-scribble: var(--im-info)">box it</span>, or <span data-im-scribble="strike" style="--im-fx-scribble: var(--im-danger)">strike it out</span>.</p>
{{/example}}
<p><code>data-im-scribble="circle"</code> — also <code>underline</code>, <code>box</code>, <code>strike</code>. <code>im-motion.js</code> adds a hand-drawn SVG path stretched to the phrase (so it fits any words at any size) and the pen <strong>draws it in</strong> when it scrolls into view. <code>--im-fx-scribble</code> is the ink (the accent by default); <code>--im-fx-stroke</code> its weight. Keep the phrase on one line — a circle cannot wrap.</p>

<h2>Wiggle, wave, breathe</h2>
<p>Per-letter motion. The letters must be split: add <code>data-im-split="chars"</code>.</p>
{{#example}}
<p class="text-display font-semibold tracking-tighter"><span class="im-fx-wiggle" data-im-split="chars">Wiggle</span> · <span class="im-fx-wave" data-im-split="chars">Wave</span></p>
<p class="text-display tracking-tighter mt-4"><span class="im-fx-breathe" data-im-split="chars">Breathe in, breathe out</span></p>
<p class="text-h2 font-semibold tracking-tight mt-6"><span class="im-fx-wiggle im-fx-hover" data-im-split="chars">Only when hovered — add im-fx-hover</span></p>
{{/example}}
<div class="im-table-scroll">
<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Class</th><th></th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td><code>im-fx-wiggle</code></td><td>Each letter rocks, out of step with its neighbours.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-fx-wave</code></td><td>A wave passes along the word.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-fx-breathe</code></td><td>Each letter's <strong>weight</strong> swells and thins in turn — possible only because Geist is a variable font.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-fx-hover</code></td><td>Runs only while hovered.</td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>A screen reader still gets the word whole: the letters are hidden from it and the element is labelled with the full text.</p>

<h2>Stack</h2>
{{#example}}
<p class="text-display font-bold tracking-tighter"><span class="im-fx-stack">Poster lettering.</span></p>
{{/example}}
<p>A hard, stepped shadow in the accent. Sized in <code>em</code>, so it scales with the type.</p>

<h2>Pixel</h2>
{{#example}}
<p class="text-display tracking-tight"><span class="im-pixel">Geist Pixel, </span><span class="font-semibold">beside Geist.</span></p>
{{/example}}
<p>Not an effect so much as a voice: <code>im-pixel</code> sets Geist Pixel. One word or one line in a heading is the dose.</p>

<h2>Typewriter</h2>
{{#example}}
<p class="text-h2"><span class="im-fx-typewriter" data-replay style="--im-fx-chars: 28">npm install im-design-system</span></p>
{{/example}}
<p>Types itself once, with a caret. It is set in Geist Mono because it <em>needs</em> a monospaced face — the reveal is counted in characters: <code>style="--im-fx-chars: 28"</code>.</p>
<p>The count only has to be <em>close</em>. The width is borrowed for the length of the animation and given back afterwards (<code>animation-fill-mode: backwards</code>), so a count that is short makes the last few letters arrive in one step rather than clipping them off the end for good — which is how this used to fail, silently, and why the demo above was missing two characters.</p>

<h2>Glitch</h2>
{{#example}}
<p class="text-display font-bold tracking-tighter"><span class="im-fx-glitch" data-text="Signal lost">Signal lost</span></p>
{{/example}}
<p>Two offset, clipped copies flicker now and then. It needs the text a second time, in <code>data-text</code>. Use sparingly: it is the loudest thing here.</p>

<h2>Split reveal</h2>
<p><code>data-im-split="words"</code> (or <code>"chars"</code>): <code>im-motion.js</code> wraps each unit so the text arrives piece by piece when it scrolls into view. Screen readers still get the sentence whole — the pieces are hidden from them and the element is labelled with the full text.</p>
{{#example}}
<h3 class="text-display font-semibold tracking-tighter" data-im-split="words" style="max-width: 16ch">Every word arrives on its own beat.</h3>
<p class="im-pixel text-h1 text-ink mt-6" data-im-split="chars" style="--im-fx-split-step: 35ms">CHARACTER BY CHARACTER</p>
{{/example}}

<h2>Scramble</h2>
{{#example}}
<p class="font-mono text-h2 text-ink" data-im-scramble>Resolving out of noise…</p>
{{/example}}
<p><code>data-im-scramble</code>: the text resolves, left to right, out of random glyphs when revealed. Monospace keeps it from jittering.</p>

<h2>Orbit</h2>
<p>A ring of type that turns, with the logo's recording dot at its centre — a seal at the end of an about page, "open for work" round an avatar, "scroll" under a hero. The letters are set on the path by the browser's own text engine, so they sit on the curve exactly and stay crisp at any size; nothing here rotates one letter at a time and hopes.</p>
{{#example center=true style="padding-block: 2.5rem"}}
<div class="im-cluster" style="--im-cluster-gap: 3rem; align-items: center">
	{{> "components/orbit" id="orbit-a" text="Im Design System · Tailwind 4 · Ghost 6 · "}}
	{{> "components/orbit" id="orbit-b" shape="square" text="Read the journal · Read the journal · " speed="26s" back=true style="--im-orbit-dot-color: var(--im-ink)"}}
	{{#> "components/orbit" id="orbit-c" text="Open for work · Open for work · " size="7.5rem" speed="14s"}}{{> "components/avatar" size="lg" src=demo.author.profile_image name=demo.author.name}}{{/"components/orbit"}}
</div>
{{/example}}
<div class="im-table-scroll">
<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Param</th><th></th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td><code>id</code></td><td>Required, and unique on the page — the <code>&lt;textPath&gt;</code> points at it.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>text</code></td><td>What goes round. Repeat it yourself with separators so it fills the path.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>shape</code></td><td><code>circle</code> (default) or <code>square</code> — a rounded square path.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>size</code> · <code>speed</code> · <code>back</code></td><td>9rem, 18s, and which way it turns.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>--im-orbit-text</code></td><td>The letters' size, 0.72rem; <code>--im-orbit-tracking</code> their spacing, 0.34em. Wide tracking is what makes a ring of type read as a ring and not as a squeezed sentence.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>--im-orbit-dot</code></td><td>The centre dot, 0.5rem, in <code>--im-orbit-dot-color</code>. Put anything inside the partial instead and it replaces the dot.</td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>It stands still under <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>, and the whole ring carries one <code>aria-label</code> so a screen reader reads the words once instead of spelling a circle.</p>

<h2>Combining, and restraint</h2>
{{#example}}
<h3 class="text-display font-semibold tracking-tighter" style="max-width: 18ch">Build the theme <span class="im-fx-gradient">you would buy</span>, <span class="im-pixel">then ship it.</span></h3>
{{/example}}
<ul>
	<li><strong>One effect per headline</strong>, on a few words, not the whole line.</li>
	<li><strong>Never on body text</strong> or anything a visitor must read to proceed.</li>
	<li><strong>Looping effects (shine, glitch) at most once per view.</strong></li>
</ul>
